Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: the pending question card minimizes to a one-line
 bar
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Wave 2 of the Zeo next proposal (docs/ZEO-NEXT-PROPOSAL.md §5.5, ask 9).
Patch 0027 pins the agent's pending question above the composer, which
is right while it is being answered and costs a third of the panel while
the operator reads the conversation to decide what to answer.

A chevron on the card collapses it into one line above the composer —
"Question pending", or "Question pending · N questions" when several
wait — and the bar's chevron restores it. `agent::ToggleQuestionCard`
does the same from the keyboard (no default binding), and both controls
carry an accessible label and a tooltip naming the action.

The state lives on the ThreadView, so it is per thread, and it returns
to open as soon as no question is pending: the next question must never
arrive hidden. The questions themselves are untouched while minimized —
still pending, still blocking the turn — and 0043's Enter rule is
unchanged.

Tests: thread_view tests/question_card_minimize_tests.rs — the card
minimizes to the bar and comes back; a minimized card is open again once
the question is answered. Verified 2026-11-09 in the prepared d2a4fb6
tree: cargo check --tests, cargo clippy --tests and cargo fmt --check
clean on agent_ui; the 79 elicitation tests still pass. The bar's look
is for an Xvfb capture.
